breaking tonight what was supposed to be  a Labor Day adventure has turned into a  deadly nightmare for people on a  chartered diving boat off the coast of  California at least four are dead and 29  more are missing after a devastating  early morning fire corresponding  Christina Coleman is live in Los Angeles  tonight good evening Christina  good evening Mike well a frantic search  is underway for more than two dozen  people after this diving ship burst into  flames early this morning forcing the  ship's crew members to jump overboard  four bodies have been recovered so far  the Coast Guard saying their injuries  were consistent with drowning take a  listen to the dispatcher on the Mayday  call when the deadly fire was reported  you can't hear how the crew member is  responding but it sure gives you a sense  of the situation  [Applause]  Coast Guard harbor patrol officers  helicopters all rushed to the scene once  the call came in around 3:30 this  morning 39 people were aboard the diving  ship Concepcion including five crew  members who all made it off the 75 foot  boat near Santa Cruz Island a Coast  Guard officer says people were below  deck asleep  however those five crew members were  awake and above deck and able to jump  off the ship  two of them suffering minor injuries a  Good Samaritan let them onto their boat  to get them to safety the Concepcion st.  just 20 yards offshore in 64 feet of  water while firefighters were trying to  put out that fire we managed to get  video of a rescued man brought ashore  alert and talking to first responders  the dive boat was on the last day of a  Labor Day weekend cruise to the Channel  Islands about 70 miles north of Los  Angeles loved ones gathered at the  harbor in Santa Barbara where the  conception was based hoping for good  news this man just found out his brother  a cook on the boat had escaped usually  he's making breakfast at 4:00 in the  morning  so something happened he got off of the  boat seized one of the survivors so I'm  going in here to talk to him right now  California Senator Dianne Feinstein once  answer she released a statement just  moments ago saying the FBI and NTSB will  be investigating the Coast Guard says an  early look at the boats records show it  is in compliance with state laws and  that the owner of the boat is  cooperating with investigators Mike  Christina Coleman live in LA Christina  thanks a lot
 

